# Auth

- Browser client: `lib/supabase/client.ts`. Return `null` when env vars are missing — never crash the marketing site.
- Server session: `lib/supabase/server.ts`. Refresh cookies in `proxy.ts` (Next.js 16 middleware).
- Env: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`. Document in `.env.example` only. Never commit real keys.
- Sign-in dialog: password, magic link, and **Continue with Google**. Do not ask seeker vs provider. Role comes from the page: `/for-providers` → `provider`, everywhere else → `seeker` (`audienceFromPath` in `lib/site.ts`). Signup and Google pass that role into metadata / `/auth/callback?role=`. Existing accounts keep their role.
- Google needs the provider enabled in Supabase (Auth > Providers) plus `http://localhost:3000/auth/callback` on the redirect allow list. The app callback exchanges the PKCE `code`.
- If Supabase is not configured, submit still explains that clearly with a toast. Do not fake a session.
- No sensitive detail in toasts or lock-screen copy. Magic-link email should stay generic.
- Later: PIN/biometric, quick-hide, and export/delete belong in the app shell, not this dialog.
